<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 11 May, from 868 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">868 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Diamond Sutra is printed in Tang China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A block-printed copy of the Diamond Sutra was made on this date, according to its colophon. Found in a cave at Dunhuang, it is the oldest dated printed book known.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1502 CE <span class="tih-ago">524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sails from Cádiz on his fourth voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Christopher Columbus set out on his last voyage, exploring the coast of Central America from Honduras to Panama. Shipwrecked on Jamaica for a year, he returned to Spain in 1504.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1745 CE <span class="tih-ago">281 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marshal Saxe defeats the allied army at Fontenoy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French forces under Maurice de Saxe beat British, Dutch and Hanoverian troops led by the Duke of Cumberland. The victory opened the way to the French conquest of the Austrian Netherlands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1812 CE <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prime Minister Spencer Perceval is shot in the Commons lobby</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Bellingham, a merchant with a grievance against the government, shot Perceval dead. He remains the only British prime minister to be assassinated.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1857 CE <span class="tih-ago">169 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mutinous sepoys from Meerut seize Delhi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebel soldiers rode into Delhi and proclaimed the aged Mughal emperor Bahadur Shah II their leader. The Indian Rebellion that spread from here led to the end of East India Company rule in 1858.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-ii">Bahadur Shah II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1998 CE <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">India conducts nuclear tests at Pokhran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">India detonated three nuclear devices in the Rajasthan desert, followed by two more on 13 May, and declared itself a nuclear weapons state. Pakistan responded with its own tests within weeks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
